    "minides": "The longest Defender ever — 5358mm, 8 seats across 3 full-adult rows, 3022mm wheelbase, and the same 900mm wading and Terrain Response 2 as the 90 and 110. Available in D300 diesel mild-hybrid or 518 PS V8.",
    "description": "The Defender 130 is the extended-wheelbase, 3-row version of the Defender 110, adding 340mm of length for a dedicated third row of adult-sized seats. In India it is offered in two variants — D300 (₹1.45 Cr, diesel mild-hybrid, 8 seats) and V8 P500 (₹1.86 Cr, 518 PS supercharged V8, 7 seats). The 130 shares the 3022mm wheelbase with the 110 but has a longer 5358mm overall length and a unique overhanging rear design to accommodate the third row. Boot space in 8-seat configuration is 389 litres, expanding massively with the third row folded. All off-road hardware — 900mm water wading, air suspension, twin-speed transfer case, Terrain Response 2 — is carried over unchanged. The 2025 update brings the 13.1-inch Pivi Pro Gen 2 and improved cabin refinement."
  },
